 cerevisiae</italic> co-crystalized with an antibody F<sub>v</sub> fragment</article-title>. <source>Structure</source> <volume>8</volume>, 669&#x02013;684.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10873857</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ref6"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal" id="cit6"><name><surname>Berry</surname><given-names>E. A.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>L.-S.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Saechao</surname><given-names>L. K.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Pon</surname><given-names>N. G.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Valkova-Valchanova</surname><given-names>M. B.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Daldal</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name>  (<year>2004</year>) <article-title>X-ray structure of <italic>Rhodobacter capsulatus</italic> cytochrome <italic>bc</italic><sub>1</sub>: comparison with its mitochondrial and chloroplast counterparts</article-title>. <source>Photosynth. Res.</source> <volume>81</volume>, 251&#x02013;275.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16034531</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ref7"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal" id="cit7"><name><surname>Esser</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Elberry</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Zhou</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>C. A.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Xia</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name>  (<year>2008</year>) <article-title>Inhibitor-complexed structures of the cytochrome <italic>bc</italic><sub>1</sub> from the photosynthetic bacterium <italic>Rhodobacter sphaeroides</italic></article-title>. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>283</volume>, 2846&#x02013;2857.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18039651</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ref8"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal" id="cit8"><name><surname>Kurisu</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>J. L.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Cramer</surname><given-names>W. A.</given-names></name>  (<year>2003</year>) <article-title>Structure of the cytochrome <italic>b</italic><sub>6</sub><italic>f</italic> complex of oxygenic photosynthesis: tuning the cavity</article-title>. <source>Science</source> <volume>302</volume>, 1009&#x02013;1014.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14526088</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ref9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal" id="cit9"><name><surname>Stroebel</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Choquet</surname><given-names>Y.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Popot</surname><given-names>J.-L.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Picot</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name>  (<year>2003</year>) <article-title>An atypical haem in the cytochrome <italic>b</italic><sub>6</sub><italic>f</italic> complex</article-title>. <source>Nature</source> <volume>426</volume>, 413&#x02013;418.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14647374</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ref10"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal" id="cit10"><name><surname>Mitchell</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name>  (<year>1975</year>) <article-title>The protonmotive Q cycle: a general formulation</article-title>. <source>FEBS Lett.</source> <volume>59</volume>, 137&#x02013;139.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1227927</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ref11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal" id="cit11"><name><surname>Osyczka</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Moser</surname><given-names>C. C.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Daldal</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Dutton</surname><given-names>P. L.</given-names></name>  (<year>2004</year>) <article-title>Reversible redox energy coupling in electron transfer chains</article-title>. <source>Nature</source> <volume>427</volu